  "description": {
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Annona senegalensis",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Annona_senegalensis",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1374202364,
      "text": "Annona senegalensis, commonly known as African custard-apple, wild custard apple, wild soursop, abo ibobo, sunkungo, Gwandan daji and dorgot is a species of flowering plant in the custard apple family, Annonaceae. The specific epithet, senegalensis, translates to mean \"of Senegal\", the country where the type specimen was collected."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Annona senegalensis",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Annona_senegalensis",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 209096502,
      "text": "Le pommier cannelle du Sénégal (Annona senegalensis), est un arbuste de la famille des Annonaceae, du genre Annona, poussant dans les régions semi-arides et les zones subhumides. Son fruit, très prisé en Afrique pour ses qualités gustatives et pharmaceutiques, est appelé annone ou pomme cannelle du Sénégal."
    }
  },
